# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the tp4-serve-7 window (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it):
# copy it over .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/serve-7 and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN.
# Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a registry: the cards are resolved at run time. A placeholder in @...@ is filled
# in by whoever drives the window; every other value is final. ORDER.txt says the order, each job's image and its stop rule.
# SR7: the four-card platform replay of the NEW production image: the agent's serving sequence on all four boards (resolved at run time:
# none named) in a copy of its container running the THIN LAYER image (@THIN_LAYER_IMAGE@: the platform image built on tp4-serve-7 and
# pre-pulled into the rig daemon, given by digest). C2_REPLAY_PROFILE is the four-card traffic profile the copy must BOOT by the image
# default: the agent forwards no QWEN_C2_PROFILE, so the replay sets none either; the served model is left at its default,
# Qwen/Qwen3.8-27B:tt. Each boot's (load, reload, restart) vLLM subprocess log - the runtime's /tmp/thatch_vllm_N.log, read from the
# container, never docker logs - must show '[QWEN-C2] profile c2-packed-tp4: vLLM argv', the P150x4 mesh line, admission passed with no
# UNQUALIFIED, parser M armed, 'extent replay engaged' and the prefill warm checks; the n=2 edge refusal is judged strictly because the
# contract line is read from that log. This is the shape that hung with the audits off before the in-trace sampler (SR v163): the
# replay's traffic step is the first four-user answers' tail, and it must now complete. The source record's image must be present in
# the rig daemon (the replay subtracts its ENV; without it the replay refuses before docker run). The restart step (docker stop with
# the teardown skipped, then docker start) is the first reopening of the four-card mesh after an unclean exit: a wedge there FAILS the
# replay and blocks placement; the next job (H7) begins with the quad reset and heals.
# Duration (estimate): 35 min, then H7's quad reset and the platform's fabric re-measure. Stop rule: any FAIL stops placement.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset replay
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-serve-7
C2_PLATFORM_IMAGE=@THIN_LAYER_IMAGE@
C2_REPLAY_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4
